{
  "key": "income-tax.tds-threshold-limits",
  "title": "TDS threshold limits of the Income-tax Act, 2025",
  "description": "The threshold limits of sections 392 and 393 of the Income-tax Act, 2025, in force from 1 April 2026, one row for each case a limit distinguishes: the limit as printed, its amount in rupees, the test and how the Act measures the amount. A limit printed as Nil is 0 with the test that the amount exceeds it, so every amount is deducted; a limit printed without a figure has no amount. The limit of section 393(1) [Table: Sl. No. 3(i)] follows its Note 3, as the Finance Act, 2026, section 84(a), amended it: tax is deducted where the consideration or the stamp duty value is equal to or greater than fifty lakh rupees.",
